WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.770
Fire a slow neutron at
a uranium-235 nucleus.

2
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:10.050
The nucleus absorbs it, wobbles,
then splits into two smaller nuclei,

3
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.910
barium and krypton, plus 3 spare neutrons.

4
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.870
The fragments fly apart,
carrying a burst of energy.

5
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.530
That seems backwards.

6
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:22.300
Pulling things apart
normally takes effort.

7
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.940
So how can breaking a
nucleus apart release energy?

8
00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:28.890
In this mission, you'll
balance a fission equation,

9
00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:32.890
counting every nucleon and
every proton on both sides.

10
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:38.480
Then you'll meet californium-252, a
nucleus that can split all on its own,

11
00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:40.440
with no neutron needed.

12
00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:44.670
Your mission: explain how splitting
a nucleus can release energy.
